{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Working Hard"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Stress Management"}, {"type": "position", "content": 6}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Analyze issues relating to different topics and their solution in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to restore "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200breturn something or someone to an \u200bearlier good \u200bcondition or \u200bposition"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Restore work-life balance."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about solving problems."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "meditation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the \u200bact of giving \u200byour \u200battention to only one thing as a way of \u200bbecoming \u200bcalm and \u200brelaxed"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are different types of meditation techniques that can calm your mind and reduce your stress."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob06aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to minimize "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make less"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are 8 proven ways to minimize stress and limit its health effects."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "optimism"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the \u200bquality of being \u200bfull of \u200bhope and \u200ba \u200bbelief that something good will \u200bhappen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Studies indicate that optimism or pessimism affects your quality of life."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to visualize "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to \u200bform a \u200bpicture of someone or something in \u200byour \u200bmind, in \u200border to \u200bimagine it "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Concentration meditation involves focusing your attention on one thing, such as your breathing or an image you visualize."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to alter "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "  to \u200bchange something, usually \u200bslightly, or to \u200bcause the \u200bcharacteristics of something to \u200bchange"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are four ways that can help manage stress: avoid, alter, adapt or accept!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to keep your cool "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to remain calm"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You've got to keep your cool."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob06aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le09ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Relative Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You use relative clauses to make your writing and speaking more detailed and sophisticated. A defining clause gives essential information about a noun. A non-defining clause gives additional information about a noun."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In relative clauses, you use <span class=\"italic\">who</span> for people, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> or <span class=\"italic\">which</span> for things, <span class=\"italic\">when</span> with time and <span class=\"italic\">where</span> with places. <br/><br/>  <span class=\"underline\">Defining Clause</span>: <br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">People <span class=\"strong\">who talk too much</span> annoy me a lot.</span><br/><br/>  Without the clause \u201cwho talk too much\u201d, the meaning of the sentence changes: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">People annoy me a lot. </span><br/><br/>  <span class=\"underline\">Non-defining Clause:</span><br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">My younger sister, <span class=\"strong\">who is really shy</span>, rarely speaks to anyone.</span><br/><br/>  Without the clause \u201cwho is really shy\u201d the main idea of the sentence stays the same. <br/> You use commas to separate the non-defining clause from the rest of the sentence.<br/><br/>  Look at some examples from the dialogue:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Studies indicate that optimism or pessimism affects your quality of life."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Positive strategies which deal with stress help avoid negative consequences."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are different types of meditation techniques that can calm your mind and reduce your stress."}, {"type": "example", "content": "A strong social support network is made up of friends, family and peers who can help you through periods of stress. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are four ways that can help manage stress: avoid, alter, adapt or accept!"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Stress Management Tips"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " Some workplace stress is normal. However, excessive stress can interfere with your workflow and influence your physical and emotional health. Your ability to cope with it can mean the difference between success or failure."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can't control everything in your work environment, but that doesn't mean you're helpless. Finding ways to manage workplace stress isn't about making huge changes or rethinking career ambitions, but rather about focusing on the one thing that's always within your control: you.<br/><br/>  Read the following tips to manage workplace stress:"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should think positively."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You had better change your emotional response."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You ought to think about stress as your reaction to an event, rather than the event itself. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "You need to take time for yourself without feeling guilty."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should try meditation."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You've got to keep your cool."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You need to maintain a strong social network."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, brainstorm all the ways you can reduce stress in your life."}, {"type": "text", "content": "On your own, choose 10 of your ideas and put them in order from most effective to least effective."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a short description for each tip."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compare your list with your partner. Do you have many differences in your lists?"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I brainstorm ways to reduce stress."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a list of tips for reducing stress."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I put my list in order from most effective to least effective."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I compare my list with my partner."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le09ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le09ob06re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le09ob06re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">8 Proven Ways to Minimize Stress and Limit its Health Effects</span></br></br>\n<ol start=\"1\"><li>You should think positively<br>\nStudies indicate that optimism or pessimism affects your quality of life. Optimism enables you to cope better with stressful situations and reduce the effects of stress on your body.</li>\n<li>You had better change your emotional response<br>\nPositive strategies which deal with stress help avoid negative consequences. You ought to think about stress as your reaction to an event, rather than the event itself.</li></ol>", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le09ob06re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<ol start=\"3\"><li>Protect your time<br>\nSome people find it hard to say no to the requests which are made of their time. But saying yes to everything comes at a price \u2014 more stress and less peace of mind. You need to take time for yourself without feeling guilty.</li>\n<li>Restore work-life balance<br>When your work life and personal life feel out of balance, stress \u2014 plus its harmful effects \u2014 is the result.</li>\n<li>You should try meditation<br>\nThere are different types of meditation techniques that can calm your mind and reduce your stress. Concentration meditation involves focusing your attention on one thing, such as your breathing or an image you visualize.</li></ol>", "id": 2, "time": "32000", "image": "engenn10le09ob06re2img06.jpg "}, {"text": "<ol start=\"6\"><li>You've got to keep your cool<br> Focus on what you can do to gain control of the situation.<br> There are four ways that can help manage stress: avoid, alter, adapt or accept!</li>\n<li>You need to maintain a strong social network<br> A strong social support network is made up of friends, family and peers who can help you through periods of stress. <br> A social support network is something that you should develop when you're not under stress, providing the comfort of knowing that your friends are there if you need them.</li></ol>", "id": 3, "time": "78000", "image": "engenn10le09ob06re2img07.jpg "}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type":